sweeping W = 129..=768 (the wide rung, three 128-bit periods)

W values in 129..=768 where Hot's byte count equals Warm's (no padding needed): 40 of 640
first witness: W = 249, byte count = 32 for both Hot and Warm

at this W, both declarations have IDENTICAL (W, stride):
  W = 249, stride = 256 bits, for BOTH Hot and Warm

compiled, const-checked witness at W = 256:
  Warm carrier: WideBits<32>            size  32  align  1
  Hot  carrier: AlignedWideBits16<32>    size  32  align 16
  same declared width (256), same stride (256 bits), same byte count (32).
  different carrier TYPE (different alignment).

so the pair (W, stride) does NOT determine carrier, at 40 of 640 wide-rung
widths in this sweep, with ZERO dependence on Precise and ZERO dependence on sign.
this collision arises purely from Hot's align-16 wide-rung padding coinciding with
Warm's align-1 unpadded byte count at widths where the byte count already happens
to be a multiple of 16.

negative control: at a width where the byte counts genuinely differ, no collision.
  W = 240: Warm bytes = 30, Hot bytes = 32. Different strides, no collision at this W.
